"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative focused on implementing AI algorithms to increase efficiency by 20%, with a prototype for secure file sharing already tested ahead of schedule. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research and expanded its team with experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Initially approved with a $2M budget, the budget was later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses to cover real-time analytics integration. Key upcoming events include a meeting on August 5th to discuss initial findings, UI enhancements starting in October, and new security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January next year. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November."
